From: Automation Platform controller <controller@pipefail.dev>
Subject: [PATCH 0015] yield dispatch workers while organization jobs cancel

Fixes F309. The resumable organization-deletion reaper held one dispatcherd
worker for up to 300 seconds while polling canceled jobs. Cleanup bursts could
therefore consume every worker, leaving project updates and learner jobs queued
until their clients timed out.

Cancellation is still requested idempotently, but an active job now causes the
reaper to persist progress and return its worker immediately. The existing
database-backed 20-second pump re-admits cancelling rows, so the wait remains
durable across task-process restarts without occupying task capacity.

Tested by: awx/main/tests/unit/test_org_deletion.py and the controller patch
apply/syntax tripwire. Deployed concurrency proof remains required.

